<bblocks://ogc.contrib.stac.extensions.eo> a skos:Concept,
        dcat:Dataset,
        bblocks:BBlock,
        bblocks:Schema ;
    rdfs:label "STAC Electro-Optical Extension" ;
    dct:abstract """Electro-Optical (EO) Extension to the SpatioTemporal Asset Catalog (STAC) specification.

EO data is considered to be data that represents a snapshot of the Earth for a single date and time. It could consist of multiple spectral bands in any part of the electromagnetic spectrum. Examples of EO data include sensors with visible, short-wave and mid-wave IR bands (e.g., the OLI instrument on Landsat-8), long-wave IR bands (e.g. TIRS aboard Landsat-8)."""^^<https://www.w3.org/ns/iana/media-types/text/markdown> ;
    dct:created "2023-12-08T00:00:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dct:description [ dct:format "application/json" ;
            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ogcincubator.github.io/bblocks-stac/build/generateddocs/json-full/contrib/stac/extensions/eo/index.json> ],
        [ dct:format "text/markdown" ;
